# ── External-compute boundary pins ────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# KIND: MECHANISM pin — fixture inline by design, see pins/rights-floor.nibli.
#
# Run by `just verify-pins` (nibli-pin, native).
#
# WHAT THIS GUARDS. A relation becomes a ComputeNode at COMPILE time, against the
# session's live registry — so registration ORDER used to be load-bearing:
#
#   exponential(2, 3, 8).   asserted BEFORE `:compute exponential` — stored as an
#                           ordinary fact no compute query would ever consult
#                           again; listed, retractable, unreachable forever.
#
# The closure is BOTH-ENDED (decided 2026-08-09). The REFERENCE external names
# (`exponential`, `logarithm` — nibli-types REFERENCE_EXTERNAL_COMPUTE) are
# query-only at assertion ingress in every position, registered or not: unlike
# greater/less/num_equal there is NO relational reading to protect — every
# committed place is numeric (result/base/power; result/number/base) — so for
# these two names the NAME is the operand test and nothing is collateral. And
# registration itself is fallible and corpus-scoped: it is routing metadata,
# not a vocabulary/arity declaration, and is refused while live stored facts or
# rules reference the canonical relation, with the blocking ids in the message
# — retract first.
#
# DECIDED, NOT DEFERRED (2026-08-09). Accept-and-disclose was declined: a KB
# whose facts silently stop being consulted halfway through a session is the
# assert/query divergence class the comparison guard closes, minus the guard.
# Re-open trigger: a corpus or import source that needs either name as ordinary
# relational vocabulary, or a configurable reference set — either turns the
# static name list into policy and would need an operand-style test instead.
# GUARANTEES §Compute Result Lifecycle and §Disclosed Sharp Edges carry the
# contract.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE CANNOT PIN. The pin language has no registration directive and
# its engine is immutable, so REGISTRATION ORDER — refusal over live references,
# success after retraction, both orders — is pinned in Rust
# (`assert_then_register_is_refused_until_the_statements_are_retracted` and
# `an_external_compute_name_is_query_only_even_before_registration`,
# nibli-engine) and across the WIT boundary by the
# `smoke-host-compute-registration-order` gate. Do not read this file as
# covering it.

# ── THE REFERENCE NAMES ARE REFUSED IN EVERY ASSERTED POSITION, UNREGISTERED ──
# The pin engine registers nothing, so every refusal below is the STATIC name
# guard — the exact pre-fix hole. All five carry the same needle, so a typo (a
# Syntax error) cannot satisfy them.

# A ground fact. Pre-fix this stored and answered TRUE — until any session
# registered the name, after which it was unreachable but still listed.
:refuse reasoning /reserved for EXTERNAL COMPUTE/
exponential(8, 2, 3).

# The other reference name, same contract.
:refuse reasoning /reserved for EXTERNAL COMPUTE/
logarithm(3, 8, 2).

# A positive rule guard.
:refuse reasoning /reserved for EXTERNAL COMPUTE/
all $x: all $n: person($x) & quantity($x, $n) & exponential($n, 2, 3) -> fit($x).

# A NEGATED rule guard — the overfiring one: an empty stored extension under `~`
# succeeds for every binding.
:refuse reasoning /reserved for EXTERNAL COMPUTE/
all $x: all $n: person($x) & quantity($x, $n) & ~exponential($n, 2, 3) -> rotten($x).

# A rule HEAD.
:refuse reasoning /reserved for EXTERNAL COMPUTE/
all $x: all $n: quantity($x, $n) -> exponential($n, 2, 3).

# ── ORDINARY VOCABULARY IS NOT COLLATERAL DAMAGE ──────────────────────────────
# The ban is two exact names (role spellings collapse onto them), not a pattern.

:accept
person(Adam).

? person(Adam).
# => TRUE

# ── THE UNREGISTERED QUERY READING ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Assertion is closed by NAME; the QUERY side still follows the registry. In
# this never-registered engine the stored extension is necessarily empty, so
# the closed-world answer is FALSE — decided, not an error. (A REGISTERED
# session dispatches the backend instead; that half lives in the Rust pins.)

? exponential(8, 2, 3).
# => FALSE

# ── OPAQUE QUOTED CONTENT STAYS INERT ─────────────────────────────────────────
# A belief ABOUT a computation is not a stored computation.

:accept
believe(me, fact { exponential(8, 2, 3) }).

? believe(me, fact { exponential(8, 2, 3) }).
# => TRUE

:expect-pins 10
